Z||000000||filthyscarecrow||03-14-2001||12:33 AM||||hey, anyone in here play with r/c cars? i used to race them when i was a kid. my dad was my pit crew. he was an awesome pit crew. <P>i guess i just miss him. <P>i have an HPI touring car that i bought to race, but never got around to it. bigger better projects (formula SAE). i'd still liek to race it though. i also have a 1/10 ferrari (actually williams painted like a ferrari) f-1 car. both are fun, but the HPI is easier to drive seein as how it's 4WD. you can drift through corners on hardwood floors. the SAE guys got a huge kick out of it. <P>seriously though, aside from your fieros, what kind of toys do you like? <P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...||||reg||5
Z||000001||Loki||03-14-2001||12:52 AM||||LEGOS!!!!!! Lots and lots of Legos...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||03-14-2001||12:55 AM||||I wanted to do the R/C thing, but never really got started on it.  Was spending all my money on my mountain bikes at the time.  Of course, my 2 mountain bikes are worth more than both my Fiero's put together... got my Independent Fabrications race bike and my Kona U'Hu play bike.  'Bout the only toys I have other than my spud guns and my Fiero's, of course  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||03-14-2001||01:43 AM||||I was into R/C's when I was a kid too.<P>My father and I started out racing on indoor road course carpet tracks with Associated 12L pan cars running GTP IMSA type bodies.  Eventually we got into the bigger 10L's running NASCAR bodies.  One time we raced at a <B>huge</B> cement oval track in King NC.  Hehe, those things were so fast, guys were smacking the walls and snapping 1/4" dia. carbon graphite axles like nothing.  The axles on our cars were titanium.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  We ran some 12L's again with sprint car midget bodies on indoor ovals, now those were fun.<P>A couple years ago, a slot car road course track opened in my town.  I raced, but this time I was the pit crew for my little sister.  She ran in a NASCAR league for the kids, she did well but mainly had a lot of fun.  I raced NASCAR and NASCAR truck series bodied slot cars.  Originally, I was only going to race the NASCAR bodied cars, but a neighbor I knew offered to let me run his practice truck for the first season race for the truck league.  Hehe, I beat the guy with his own practice truck and won the race.  Since I won, I had to race in both leagues.   Built my own truck for the second race.  Went on to win all 10 or so races that season   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">.  Also raced with a friend and won a 4 hour endurance race in the dark!  Lol, everyone had to hook up a small halogen bulb on their car so that the current from the track would light it when you'd give it go, it would turn off everytime you let off for a corner making the race extremely interesting.  Unfortunatly the owner closed the place about a year or so after it opened.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I've been looking to get back into R/C or slot car racing again soon, its a lot of fun!<P>Lego's were fun, only until Mom found one with the vacuum cleaner.  Sorry Mom.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 03-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||03-14-2001||02:43 AM||||If I had an R/C it would be an airplane.  <BR>The only things like toys I now have are my nunchakus and my juggling clubs.<P>I know a hardware store in Ohio that hosts belt sander races, but I never went to see it.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 03-14-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000005||1FST2M6||03-14-2001||08:22 AM||||I was on the local R/C pulling Circuit when i was in school.. i had a 2wd Tamiya Black foot that would pull 385lbs about 30'!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I've got a Tamiya TA-03RS, the ol blackfoot, an RC10GT, and run with a friends HPI RS4 Nitro with a Celica and the Peugeot body... <P>BlackGT (todd green) has a scratch built drag car that'll run the 132' in 1.6 seconds at 59mph!!! it's SOOO sweet! He's on the regional 1/10 scale drag circuit. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||03-14-2001||09:10 AM||||What kind of toys to I like?<P>Swords.  Definately swords.  Lot's of steel to play with.  Did I mention I like swords?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I tinker with computers, but that's not really a hobby, although it should be.  My Fiero is my primary hobby, but I'm also into photography.  When I was a kid, the best toy ever was Legos, hands down.  I've still got mine, but I don't play with them much anymore.<P>Anyone know where I can buy Legos in bulk?  I want to build an entire floor to ceiling fireplace for my gameroom out of Legos.  Complete with clear Lego flames and backlighting, and a useable mantle.  Suggestions?  Just call up Lego, "I'd like to by 10,000 red Lego's, please.  And 1000 white ones, for the morter."  That would be a funny converstation.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000007||bHooper||03-14-2001||09:36 AM||||it started with Lincoln Logs, then it was Tinker Toys, and along came Erector Sets, but nothing, absolutely nothing beat LEGO'S!<P>i had enough legos, that i would design and build space ships, with as many as 4 decks, crew quarters, engine rooms, etc.  these things would be like 4-5 foot long and up to a foot wide!<P>my grandma also gave me a chemistry set for my 12th birthday... mwahhhaahaa... <B>mistake</B>... as far as the tad poles, frogs and fish of my parents pond, were concerned, it was definately a Jr. Mad Scientist kit!<P>very interesting, the things that i created with that... and who knows what still lerks in that part of the county??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000008||LZeitgeist||03-14-2001||09:45 AM||||Man, I never knew so many other people were as obsessed with Legos as *I* was growing up!!! Legos ROCK!!!<P>I have to second that swords thing up there... been performing stage combat for ten years... swords are *definitely* a cool toy when you know how to impress the chicks with them safely. :::chuckle:::<P>Hey, anyone remember 'Jokari'? "Raquetball without the walls"?  I just got one from eBay, but I'm nervous to try it out because the rubber band and ball may be too old to survive... I'll have to try it out this summer, I guess.<P>||||reg||1
